<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Karnal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1739">1739</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Karnal · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shahs-invasion-of-india">Nader Shah's invasion of India</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Karnal was fought in 1739 north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nader-shah">Nader Shah</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and the Mughal emperor Muhammad Shah. Nader's army won a decisive victory, and he went on to occupy and plunder Delhi, taking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peacock-throne">Peacock Throne</a>. The campaign brought great wealth to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afsharid-empire">Afsharid Empire</a> and exposed Mughal weakness.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-karnal.jpg" alt="Battle of Karnal" width="320" height="281" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Amir Pashaei · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_painting_in_Chehel_Sotoun2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
